{"title":"Swift Bare Bones","slug":"Swift_Bare_Bones","html":"<div class=\"wk-note wk-warn\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-note-label\">Read first</span></p>\n<p>Before this page: have you read <a data-wiki=\"Getting Started\" href=\"#/library/Getting_Started\">Getting Started</a>, <a data-wiki=\"Beginner Mistakes\" href=\"#/library/Beginner_Mistakes\">Beginner Mistakes</a> and some of the <a href=\"#/library?cat=OS_theory\">OS theory</a>?</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-note wk-stub\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-note-label\">Stub</span></p>\n<p>This page on the OSDev Wiki is a stub: it covers the basics but is not complete.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-note wk-progress\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-note-label\">In progress</span></p>\n<p>This page on the OSDev Wiki is a work in progress and may be incomplete.</p>\n</div>\n<p><span class=\"wk-rating\" data-level=\"2\">Difficulty: Medium</span></p>\n<div class=\"wk-navbox\">\n<div class=\"wk-navbox-title\">\n<p><a data-wiki=\"Kernel\" href=\"#/library/Kernel\">Kernel Designs</a></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-navbox-row\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-navbox-group\">Models</span> <a data-wiki=\"Monolithic Kernel\" href=\"#/library/Monolithic_Kernel\">Monolithic Kernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Microkernel\" href=\"#/library/Microkernel\">Microkernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Hybrid Kernel\" href=\"#/library/Hybrid_Kernel\">Hybrid Kernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Exokernel\" href=\"#/library/Exokernel\">Exokernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Exokernel\" href=\"#/library/Exokernel/nanokernel_picokernel\">Nano/Picokernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Exokernel\" href=\"#/library/Exokernel/cache_kernel\">Cache Kernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Exokernel\" href=\"#/library/Exokernel/virtualizing_kernel\">Virtualizing Kernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Megalithic Kernel\" href=\"#/library/Megalithic_Kernel\">Megalithic Kernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Multikernel\" href=\"#/library/Multikernel\">Multikernel</a></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-navbox-row\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-navbox-group\">Other Concepts</span> <a data-wiki=\"Modular Kernel\" href=\"#/library/Modular_Kernel\">Modular Kernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Higher Half Kernel\" href=\"#/library/Higher_Half_Kernel\">Higher Half Kernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Creating a 64-bit kernel\" href=\"#/library/Creating_a_64_bit_kernel\">64-bit Kernel</a></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p><b>WAIT! Have you read <a data-wiki=\"Getting Started\" href=\"#/library/Getting_Started\">Getting Started</a>, <a data-wiki=\"Beginner Mistakes\" href=\"#/library/Beginner_Mistakes\">Beginner Mistakes</a>, and some of the related <a href=\"#/library?cat=OS_theory\">OS theory</a>?</b></p>\n<h2 id=\"notes\">Notes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The easiest way to use Swift is to output LLVM IR and use Clang to target the architecture you want.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"examples\">Examples</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://github.com/rzhikharevich/swift-bare-bones\" rel=\"noopener\">https://github.com/rzhikharevich/swift-bare-bones</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://github.com/klange/taylor\" rel=\"noopener\">https://github.com/klange/taylor</a></li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"notes","text":"Notes","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}],"categories":["Bare bones tutorials"],"rating":2,"flags":["stub","inprogress"],"words":135,"summary":"WAIT! Have you read Getting Started , Beginner Mistakes , and some of the related OS theory ?","updated":"2021-08-12","authors":["Sebastian"],"url":"https://wiki.osdev.org/Swift_Bare_Bones","history":"https://wiki.osdev.org/index.php?title=Swift_Bare_Bones&action=history","backlinks":[],"lessons":[]}